WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.250
My next guest is an
expert on drinking water,

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:07.200
and he's created a 40 page water menu

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.430
at Ray's and Stark Bar,
right here Los Angeles.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.900
Please welcome the country's
first water sommelier,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.763
Martin Riese.

00:00:15.941 --> 00:00:18.941
(audience applauds)

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.140
Okay, Martin, I heard about
you and I was fascinated.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.070
You're a water sommelier.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:34.903
Correct.

00:00:34.903 --> 00:00:37.750
And you believe that there
are many types of water

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.860
and flavors of water,

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.500
and it's important to
know the distinction.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.500
I'm not even believing in that.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.160
There is actually.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:43.993
It's a fact.

00:00:43.993 --> 00:00:45.200
You devoted your life to this?

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.033
Yes.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:46.866
Yes, okay.

00:00:46.866 --> 00:00:48.260
So, you must believe this.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.830
You have a degree for this.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.663
Is that correct?

00:00:50.663 --> 00:00:53.380
Correct, in 2010, I
received my certification

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.200
as a mineral water sommelier

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.600
from the German Water Association.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.433
Okay.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:01.130
So you are certified as a water sommelier.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:01.963
Correct.

00:01:01.963 --> 00:01:03.960
All right, you have a menu here.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.790
20 types of water at Ray's and Stark Bar.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.900
And I was flipping through
this and it's all these waters.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.210
Now, don't they all just taste like water?

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.387
I hate to sound ignorant.

00:01:13.387 --> 00:01:14.220
(Martin laughs)

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.980
But doesn't it just taste like water?

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.760
Uh, yes and no.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.250
So, they're all definitely water,

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.710
so they're all coming from the same, like,

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.710
source because up from the air,

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.300
because all rain water at one point.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.219
[Conan] Yes.

00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:26.830
And they're dripping down,
raining down, of the different

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.000
like sorts and different
layers of the ground.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.240
And the water going
through different layers,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.381
the same like wine, kind of.

00:01:32.381 --> 00:01:35.470
And they suddenly, they're
taking minerals with them

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.527
and so they taste differently.

00:01:36.527 --> 00:01:38.950
And you can say, like, oh
this water comes from Spain.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.100
It tastes a little bit
more like salty and bitter

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.400
than maybe water that comes
from the Fiji Islands.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.233
Yes, okay.

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.510
So, you can actually do that?

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.370
You can taste a water,

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.330
and say, yes, yes, yes,
I'm getting hints of what?

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.340
What are you getting hints of?

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.009
Saltiness, bitterness, sweetness...

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:54.842
I'm getting slate.

00:01:54.842 --> 00:01:55.675
I'm getting granite.

00:01:55.675 --> 00:01:56.600
I'm getting...

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.410
Yeah, almost like
I'm getting some mud.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:01:59.243
What am I getting here?

00:01:59.243 --> 00:02:01.420
Actually, I have one water with me today

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.253
I want you want to try.

00:02:02.253 --> 00:02:04.080
It's like a little earthy
notes to it as well.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.044
It has an earthiness?

00:02:05.044 --> 00:02:05.877
Perfect.

00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:07.260
I find this fascinating.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.860
When did you first notice that
you were fascinated by water?

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.783
I think my parents noticed it first.

00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:13.610
Because I'm coming from the Danish border,

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.090
so up north from Germany,

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.530
and when I went on
vacation with my parents,

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.690
the first thing I always
did in different cities

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.260
I was drinking tap water.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.760
And my parents was like, whoa,
what's going on with our son?

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.689
Why's he so thirsty?

00:02:24.689 --> 00:02:26.710
For me it was more like,

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.350
it's a taste, Mum.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.330
It's the taste, Dad.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.202
You don't get it?

00:02:30.202 --> 00:02:32.190
It's water, what's wrong?

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.000
We should see a doctor,
maybe or something.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:34.980
[Conan] Yes, yes.
And then like...

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.850
Yes, maybe you should see a doctor, yes.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.990
So, you were constantly drinking water,

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.620
but it was just because you
could taste different flavors.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.280
And clearly your parents couldn't, right?

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.300
They were just like, it's water.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.170
Now they can because now I explained them

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.003
a little bit as well.

00:02:49.003 --> 00:02:50.200
And I think everybody can do it.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.780
And I think even the whole
audience will, can do it as well

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.980
when they are coming to Ray's and Stark.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.380
And they will see how water
can actually taste different.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.730
Alright, we're gonna do a tasting now,

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:03.040
